From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jay Leaton <58495321+jayleaton@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 15:16:55 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 69/76] flashnext cuda: a rollback's replay in three launches
 (TF_FLASHNEXT_ROLL_BATCH), and rank waits without sleeps
 (TF_FLASHNEXT_SPIN_WAIT)

TF_FLASHNEXT_ROLL_BATCH=1 runs a partial keep's replay as fn_replay_front, fn_replay_chain and fn_late_roll over
every DeltaNet layer at once (blockIdx.z the layer), the lone launches' programs on their own slices, so the state
and conv windows come out bit for bit as the per-layer loop leaves them. TF_FLASHNEXT_SPIN_WAIT=1 drops the 50 us
sleeps from a rank's collective waits. Both default off.
